# kept — consolidated env reference (monorepo root)
#
# This file is the SINGLE documented reference for every environment variable
# across both apps. It is committed; it contains PLACEHOLDERS ONLY — never real
# secrets. Real provisioning lands in tasks 005 (Cloudflare) and 006 (Supabase).
#
# WHERE EACH APP READS ITS ENV FROM:
#   - apps/web  (control plane, Next.js): copy the relevant vars below into
#               `apps/web/.env.local` (gitignored). See apps/web/.env.example
#               for the canonical, app-scoped copy used at dev/build time.
#   - apps/edge (data plane, Cloudflare Worker): does NOT use a .env file. Its
#               non-secret config lives in `apps/edge/wrangler.toml` (R2/KV
#               bindings, routes); secrets are set via `wrangler secret put NAME`
#               and local dev vars go in `apps/edge/.dev.vars` (gitignored).
#
# SECURITY: any var prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_` is shipped to the browser. Never put
# a service-role key, S3 secret, or API token behind that prefix.

# =============================================================================
# apps/web — control plane (Next.js). Mirror of apps/web/.env.example.
# =============================================================================

# --- Supabase (required for the app to boot; auth flows wired in E2) ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-publishable-key
# Server-side service-role key (DO NOT prefix NEXT_PUBLIC_). Privileged server
# actions / route handlers only.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# --- Postgres / Drizzle (typed client; drizzle-kit migrations) ---
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@db.your-project-ref.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# --- Cloudflare R2 (object-storage writes from the control plane; task 005) ---
# The S3 API token MUST have Object Read & Write on BOTH buckets below.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=your-cloudflare-account-id
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-r2-access-key-id
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-r2-secret-access-key
# Two buckets, selected by sites.region (@kept/shared: "auto" | "eu").
# v1 writes to AUTO (sites.region defaults to "auto"); EU is dormant until E8.
R2_BUCKET_AUTO=auto-kept-sites-dev
R2_BUCKET_EU=eu-kept-sites-dev

# --- Cloudflare KV (edge manifest writes via REST; task 005) ---
# Token needs Account -> Workers KV Storage -> Edit. (Cache Purge added at E1.)
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your-cloudflare-api-token
# Namespace "kept-manifest-dev" -> its ID.
KV_NAMESPACE_ID=your-kv-namespace-id

# --- GitHub OAuth (provider configured at the Supabase project level in E2;
#     these are referenced here so the prod track is reproducible) ---
GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=your-github-oauth-client-id
GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=your-github-oauth-client-secret

# --- App ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# =============================================================================
# apps/edge — data plane (Cloudflare Worker). NOT loaded from this file.
# =============================================================================
# Bindings (non-secret) are declared in apps/edge/wrangler.toml:
#   - R2 bucket binding   KEPT_R2  -> auto-kept-sites-dev   (region "auto")
#   - KV namespace binding KEPT_KV -> kept-manifest-dev
#   - Worker route          *.kept.host/*  (zone kept.host)  [enabled in 005/E0]
# The EU bucket binding (KEPT_R2_EU) is added in E8.
#
# Worker secrets (if/when needed) are set out-of-band, NOT here:
#   wrangler secret put SOME_SECRET           # production
#   echo 'SOME_SECRET=...' >> apps/edge/.dev.vars   # local dev (gitignored)
#
# Deploying the Worker requires a Cloudflare API token with
# `Workers Scripts: Edit`. Provide it to CI as a repo/environment secret
# (CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN) — never in this file.

# =============================================================================
# CI / deploy secrets (set in GitHub Actions repo/environment secrets, NOT here)
# =============================================================================
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN     # Workers Scripts: Edit  -> apps/edge deploy (E-CI)
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID    # target account for wrangler deploy (E-CI)
# RAILWAY_TOKEN            # apps/web deploy to Railway (E-CI)
